  "limits": [
    "One/two-meter grids are not survey accuracy. Steep rock and terrain below buildings may be interpolated. Current terrace, court and entrance levels are reconstructed from surrounding open ground. No whole-site ground replacement.",
    "Working court1.6368m is0.22m above maximum sampled open court control; building floors are estimated from surrounding ground, not surveyed threshold heights.",
    "Bridge endpoints and paved north route follow fresh map geometry; the source DGM excludes bridges. The suspended approach uses reconstructed parapets and end supports, with no invented measured central arch.",
    "Outbuilding floors and widths are separately reconstructed from fresh mapped footprints and owner plans/photos. No whole-site slab, excavated ground cutout, trees, distant ruined outer ward or navigable interiors."
  ],
  "inspection": {
    "reviewedOn": "2026-10-11",
    "frames": 45,
    "notes": "All45 final normal-placement pixels actually inspected: master/four tiers at whole compound, north entrance, approach side/underspan, east/south/west elevations, courtyard, outbuildings and plan. Retained state DGM1 supplies actual ground rather than a fabricated hill. Open court is bounded and roofless; separately reconstructed floors seat the three outbuildings. The27.565m bridge and sloping paved north approach follow mapped positions; continuous parapets and exterior gate spandrels render without gaps. Coarse ground heaves beneath suspended approach; exact bridge/floor levels and acquisition date are unknown. Three outside-ground probes have0.0151m maximum fixture offset, sampled foundations and north gate void pass across five states, and five unloads release model geometry while leaving host ground intact. Inner gate remains a recess and no navigable interior is claimed."
  }
